From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH EXPERIMENTAL] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8550: add the vendor CX-retention cluster idle state

*** EXPERIMENTAL — sm8550-vendor-sleep branch until validated on device
    (armada#274). Pure DT addition; revert is clean. ***

Mainline sm8550.dtsi exposes two cluster-level domain idle states
(cluster-sleep-0 = cluster power-down 0x41000044, cluster-sleep-1 = APSS
off 0x4100c344). The vendor DTs carry a third, intermediate state between
them:

 - AYN Odin 2 firmware (odin2_20231201, base "Crow SoC" DTB in
   vendor_boot, dtbo entry 40 "Kalama SG HHG"):
     CX_RET: cx-ret {
         idle-state-name = "cx-ret";
         entry-latency-us = <1561>;  exit-latency-us = <2801>;
         min-residency-us = <8550>;
         arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x41001344>;
     };
 - CLUSTER_PD.domain-idle-states = <CLUSTER_PWR_DN CX_RET APSS_OFF>.

The LineageOS 23.2 qcs8550 base keeps only CLUSTER_PWR_DN + APSS_OFF
(0x4100c344), which matches mainline — CX_RET is optional on this
silicon, which is why it is shipped as a separate opt-out patch instead
of a dtsi rewrite.

This adds cx-ret as cluster-sleep-cxret between cluster-sleep-0 and
cluster-sleep-1 with the exact vendor latencies, and wires it into
cluster_pd's domain-idle-states. Rationale: with the qcom-lpm governor
elected (0595), an intermediate state between cluster-d4 and APSS_OFF
gives the predictor a residency-cheaper landing spot when the predicted
idle window is too short to amortize APSS_OFF's 2800/4400 us latencies —
the same ladder the vendor governor walks.

Ordering note: this patch must be applied BEFORE 0540 (system_pd), whose
cluster_pd hunk context includes the domain-idle-states line rewritten
here.

Validation (Odin 2): after boot, /sys/devices/system/cpu/cpu0/cpuidle/
must list the new state; during an s2idle soak with the qcom-lpm governor
the state usage histogram should populate between cluster-sleep-0 and
cluster-sleep-1. If the AOP silently demotes 0x41001344 (state never
entered, no errors), the state is inert but harmless — drop this patch.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
index 3962019..e3a1f7b 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8550.dtsi
@@ -373,6 +373,14 @@
 				exit-latency-us = <2350>;
 				min-residency-us = <9144>;
 			};
+
+			cluster_sleep_cxret: cluster-sleep-cxret {
+				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
+				arm,psci-suspend-param = <0x41001344>;
+				entry-latency-us = <1561>;
+				exit-latency-us = <2801>;
+				min-residency-us = <8550>;
+			};

 			cluster_sleep_1: cluster-sleep-1 {
 				compatible = "domain-idle-state";
@@ -829,7 +837,7 @@

 		cluster_pd: power-domain-cluster {
 			#power-domain-cells = <0>;
-			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_sleep_0>, <&cluster_sleep_1>;
+			domain-idle-states = <&cluster_sleep_0>, <&cluster_sleep_cxret>, <&cluster_sleep_1>;
 		};
 	};
